WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 11 - A Spring Storm

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.650
For the National Acting Competition, we will be performing:

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.840
<i>Gina and the Five Blue Jars</i>.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.190
What appears, at first glance, to be a fairy tale is actually a thriller.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.890
Gina is left alone in a house in the middle of the woods,

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:02.540
and when she opens five blue jars she's been entrusted with, she encounters a series of trials.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.590
And now, for the parts...

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.720
The lead, Gina, will be played by Maya Kitajima.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.600
"Please, come back home soon!"

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.090
"Then, tell me, girl! Quickly!"

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.730
"Did you see the man who took the jars or didn't you?!"

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:23.920
"I'm asking that you handle them with care. These jars are very important."

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.170
So, Maya Kitajima plays lead again while we're stuck in the supporting roles.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.330
You'd think we were only here to make her look good.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.090
Traveler!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.280
It's just five more days until the National Competition!

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.300
I wonder what other troupes have made it through...

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:47.600
The favorites are Tokyo's Ondine Troupe and Hokkaido's Ikkakujuu Troupe...

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.730
But, ahem... it says here that the Tsukikage Acting Troupe,

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.610
who shared first place with the Ondine Troupe may also be worthy challengers!

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.940
Hey, we're favorites to win!

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.060
Well, we'd better win then, if they so badly want us to.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.390
I dunno about all that.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.940
Hurry up and get in.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.250
Is this the place?

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.770
This is where we're staying?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.910
But there's a temple in the backyard... how creepy.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.850
That means there's a graveyard there too...

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.860
And in the middle of the night, there will be slimy, rotten...

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.510
They walked all the way from the station...

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:08.930
Left, right!

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.290
Good morning...

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.260
But it's five-thirty in the morning!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.000
Okay, all set here.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.740
Um...

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.470
What? What do you want?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.670
Oh, we were just wondering what you were up to.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.440
Oh yeah, you guys were on the same train as us yesterday.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:46.810
Yeah, we're in the Tsukikage Acting Troupe. We've come to compete in the National Acting Competition.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.850
Hurry up and get back to work!

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.890
If we don't finish up here, we won't make the performance!

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:55.200
So, are you actors too?

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.450
We're the Ikkakujuu Troupe, representing Hokkaido.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.290
Nice to meet you.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:04:59.930
Nice to meet you!

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.150
Did you say the Ikkakujuu Troupe?

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.800
You're one of the favorites!

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.550
Yeah, it's flattering. We're all still wondering how that happened.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.310
I'm Director Hotta. We're not much of a troupe, but it's nice meeting you.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:17.270
And I'm Assistant Director Keiko Ninomiya - the only girl in the troupe.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.270
And we're all glad to meet you!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:23.720
Wow!

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.610
She's never seen a guy as handsome as you before...

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.260
And now, she's all nervous.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.730
But I'm...

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.240
She's actually a girl!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.670
Then, without further ado, I will announce the running order.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:50.990
The first group to go on will be Hyogo's representative, the Hanabusa Troupe!

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.590
Next up, we have the representatives of Kanagawa, the Yokohama Troupe!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.940
The third group will be our Hokkaido team, Ikkakujuu.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:02.570
They're putting them out there on the first day, huh?

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.170
The other groups will have a hard time following that act.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:08.330
I didn't realize they were that good!

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:12.010
And on the fourth day, group twenty-five will be the Ondine Troupe.

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.710
That's strange. I wonder where they are...

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.120
I haven't seen Sakurakouji or Ayumi.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.740
Yeah, that is weird.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.770
I can't see a single person from their troupe here.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.920
And on the sixth day, group forty-three will be the Tsukikage Troupe.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:26.760
Yes, sir!

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.670
There's no need to respond.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:34.840
Yes, sir....

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:44.780
So, the Ondine Troupe never showed up.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.260
No one from their troupe has left the hotel since they arrived. Intense last-minute preparations, apparently.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:49.900
In their hotel?

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.940
Be more nimble!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.420
What are they doing?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.970
We're here to arrange for some stage time for tomorrow.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:14.960
Oh...

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.020
Ayumi's lost so much weight!

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:32.940
Careful!

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:38.730
Maya!

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.720
What's wrong, Maya?

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:47.750
It's not like you to get so down on yourself.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.530
Are you intimidated by Ayumi?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.260
Or is this about Sakurakouji?

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:59.450
It's just that... I'm such a boring person, ma'am.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.270
Compared to someone exciting like Ayumi, I'm such a butterfingers and...

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:08.490
Maya. When you're in character, there's no way you could be considered anything but exciting.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:14.220
When actors take to the stage, they have the power to take on other personalities.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.510
They can be the lively girl from town.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:21.730
They can be a queen or a fairy or even a Martian.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:27.520
There are thousands - no, tens of thousands of masks at their disposal...

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.340
and they can live more than ten thousand lives.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:35.160
Compared to the average person who only has one life to live, that's a marvelous luxury.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.110
And you have the potential to live through all of those lives.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:43.600
That is your value as a human being.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.570
My value as a human being.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.590
I can live through the stage.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:53.480
Hurry up, Maya!

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:55.140
They're running out of seats!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:01.890
Sorry... Sakurakouji!

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.610
So, we finally made it, huh?

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:05.650
Yes.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:11.480
So, tell me... I guess always being on stage with Ayumi...

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.400
means you must be pretty close or something...

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.430
Maya!

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.280
What's so funny?!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.940
That's the first time you've ever mentioned me in conversation.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:27.560
You're always so wrapped up in acting that I thought you hadn't even noticed me!

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:33.580
I haven't changed, Maya. Since the very first moment we met, I've always, always...

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.460
I've always loved you.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.970
Sakurakouji...

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:43.480
When we go head-to-head in this competition, whatever happens...

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:47.400
between our troupes, please don't forget what I just told you.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.050
We'll see each other again.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:51.390
Don't forget what I said!

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.630
They're performing <i>The Trees and the Rocks</i>!

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:28.290
Hans! Hans! Where are you going?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.470
That's Keiko?

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:32.060
She looks so... different!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.530
Please don't try and stop me, Maria.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:37.890
I'm off to Ecundra to seek my fortune!

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:43.820
Okay, Hans, but just remember that this village, this mountain, this river, this field...

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:46.470
They all love you! Hans!

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.520
You can't run away from love!

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.730
It's your destiny!

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.810
Which one of these roads leads to Ecundra?

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:02.830
All three lead to Ecundra... and yet, none of the three...

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.370
lead to Ecundra.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:09.840
If all of them lead there, then I guess I'll head right!

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:13.850
Ecundra, you say?

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.120
That's where our base is.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.710
Hop on - we'll take you there.

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.400
It's Keiko!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.050
Everyone hop on! We're going to Ecundra!

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:29.750
They play with so much spirit... you almost forget to breathe when you're watching them!

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:33.010
The blood-stained life of a murderer...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.580
awaited me at the end of the right-hand road.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:41.770
If I had taken another road at that point... I want to go back!

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:43.540
Let me go back to that fork in the road!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:49.190
Waking from my dream, I see the three roads stretching out before me again.

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:55.970
The left road led to a catastrophic life of idle love with a married countess.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:02.780
You're mine, so please, stay with me and only me!

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.280
She's changed roles again!

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.120
Keiko's played three roles now!

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.160
You murderer...

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.640
And I truly loved her!

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:19.140
At the end of the last road, I traded freedom, love and peace...

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:24.350
for fortune and fame, living a depressing life filled with boredom and irritation.

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:28.270
If destiny can be changed, I want to go back.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.500
Back to that fork in the road.

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:38.750
This... This is where the three roads fork!

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:42.940
Was this all a dream?

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.990
All three roads lead to Ecundra, and yet, none of them...

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.100
lead to Ecundra.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:53.470
Right... I'm heading back home!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:59.030
Back to the peaceful days I spent with my dear Maria!

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:02.460
This is the only road for me!

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:33.160
What? A curtain call in an acting competition?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.570
So, I guess we're on in two days.

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:41.400
I just can't stand always playing second fiddle to that little girl.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.760
Hey, you two! Can I have a word?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.770
Us... in Ondine?!

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:51.240
Yes. If you join us, you'll have your pick of TV shows, movies,

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.950
and, of course, plays. There'll be no shortage of opportunities!

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:57.920
The two of us hold you in high esteem, Mr. Onodera!

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.640
We'd do anything to be able to join your troupe!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.840
Anything, you say?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:10.830
On the fourth day, the Ondine Troupe performs <i>The Ashen Castle</i>, set in the late Meiji period.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:18.680
Once the owners of a magnificent castle, the Takinami family has now fallen destitute.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.340
Father, are you not ashamed?

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:24.050
Associating with such a woman?

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:25.880
Mia...

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:30.330
Harlot: this is not the place for you.

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:31.300
Leave now.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.380
What did you just say to me?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.900
I said, <i>leave now</i>!

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:43.610
Ayumi transforms herself into a bereft flower of a once-great family.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:49.720
Ayumi's depiction of the princess - full of haughtiness after losing her rank in the world -

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:54.400
perfectly conveys the sorrow of a ruined family.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:58.400
She's so good. Just what you'd expect from Ayumi!

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.110
Sounds like they really enjoyed it.

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:10.700
I realize how busy you are, yet here you are!

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:14.110
I had to come and see how Daito's own troupe was getting on!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:19.770
But I hear the Ikkakujuu Troupe was also extremely well-received.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.960
Not to mention our rival group, the Tsukikage Acting Troupe.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.630
Don't worry. I've already taken care of that.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.230
What do you mean by that?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.230
Mr. Genzo!

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:54.070
This is terrible!

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:57.440
Who would do such a thing?

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:58.590
Let me through.

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.300
Our costumes!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:11.180
Everything was fine when I checked them last night.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:14.830
We can't put the play on now!

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.050
Maya!

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.600
That's right! We can't just give up.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:31.620
Yes. I want all of you to help with the repairs!

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.620
We have to make it for the two o'clock performance.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:37.220
Yes... let's do it!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.840
We'll help too!

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:40.460
Leave it to us!

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:45.330
I love making props!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.130
Hey, everyone!

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.420
Good news!

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.690
We found someone who'd be willing to lend us pieces for the set and some costumes too!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:56.670
There's a high school about an hour's drive from here...

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.590
and they have the pieces of set we need.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.370
They've got costumes too! So come on!

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.120
Hop in the truck, everyone!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.780
Why don't I stay here? After all the props are fixed,

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:08.200
I'll take everyone's stuff over to the dressing room.

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.190
Sounds like a plan.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:10.460
Thanks!

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:16.440
Make sure you're in the auditorium by noon.

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.580
Got it. See you all later!

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:28.960
That's really awful, Maya...

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:31.960
That someone would come in and destroy your set and costumes...

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.230
Someone destroyed their set?

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:40.020
What have you done, Onodera?

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.220
Thank you so much for letting us borrow these.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:45.430
Good luck!

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:58.890
Great. Now it's raining...

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.690
It's great that you're doing this for me.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:16.430
What's wrong?

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:19.190
I dunno... The brakes are playing up.

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:31.020
What's taking them so long?

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.550
They should have been here hours ago!

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:37.090
What? Is there something wrong with the engine?

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:40.600
Ms. Tsukikage... your group's up soon.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:46.680
What are you doing?

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.280
Can't you fix it?

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:50.520
It's no use!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.840
I can't get a signal out here in the mountains!

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.560
You can't be serious!

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:00.940
You're trying to tell me that you're missing your set and your actors?

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:04.820
If they're not here by two o'clock, your troupe will be forced to withdraw and forfeit!

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.860
Do I make myself clear, Ms. Tsukikage?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:08.710
What are you doing?

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.530
You're going to catch cold.

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.560
Leave me alone!

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:23.650
Why? Why do these things always happen?

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.830
We've worked so hard to get here!

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.640
Go inside. You're going to fall ill.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:31.590
Please stop worrying about me!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:35.900
I know how you really feel! I bet you think this is funny, don't you?!

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.970
You're happy we can't compete!

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:42.270
Yes, you're right. You've hit the nail on the head.

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:45.390
The less rivals we have, the better... even if only one is taken out.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.510
You're horrible!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.500
How can anyone be so mean?

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:58.230
I am never, <i>ever</i> going to forgive him!

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:00.730
This is pathetic.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:05.310
Here I am, Daito's workhorse, getting soaking wet...

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.970
all for a little girl.

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.470
Maya, have they come back yet?

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:13.280
You've got ten minutes to go.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:16.000
If we don't have a set, then...

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:15.990
Wait!

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.420
If it's a set you need, we've got one right here!

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:20.460
We repaired everything we could.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:23.220
Thank you so much, you guys!

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:25.480
We're very thankful for your help!

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:28.960
Now, if only the others would get back!

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:33.650
Time's up!

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.820
You're not going to be able to perform on stage!

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:38.460
I have no choice but to pull you from the competition.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:39.670
Okay.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:41.150
I guess we have no choice.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:42.300
Wait! Please wait!

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.850
I'll do it.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:47.810
I'll go out on stage by myself.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.040
Maya!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.820
Please let me try, ma'am!

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:00.190
Even if it doesn't work, I'd like to give it a go.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:05.990
Even if I'm doomed to fail, I don't want us to surrender before we've even begun to fight!

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:10.210
And how exactly do you plan on acting out fourteen different roles?

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:15.210
If there's even the slightest, faintest, one-percent chance that I can do it...

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:18.210
I'd like to try!

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:22.800
Ma'am, please raise the curtain!

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:35.590
Surrounded by thunder and lighting, Maya makes a decision to stand alone on that stage.

00:21:35.590 --> 00:21:40.290
How can she possibly expect to act out fourteen different roles,

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:43.460
all by herself?

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:48.550
But this is just another of fate's cruel tests!

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.800
The curtain has risen on <i>Gina and the Five Blue Jars</i>...

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:27.170
and we refuse to forfeit!

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:29.430
Everyone! Please come back soon!

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:31.950
One person doesn't make a troupe!

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:36.260
I'll try to act out all the parts by myself.

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:40.910
Ms. Tsukikage, how am I doing?

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:42.800
What should I do?

00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:47.400
It's coming up to the scene where all fourteen roles appear on stage at the same time!

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 12 - Alone On Stage

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:49.100
Are you still not back yet?

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:50.730
I've reached my limit!
